  "body": "The Worker constructor has no fully-active-document requirement. Script retained from a detached iframe can therefore reach the constructor after its Window no longer has a navigable, while the algorithm still asks the user agent to derive outside settings and start a worker agent.\n\nLadybird encountered this lifecycle gap while implementing https://github.com/LadybirdBrowser/ladybird/pull/11903 and currently proposes InvalidStateError for the detached Window case.\n\nShould Worker construction require an active responsible Document, or should the standard explicitly require implementations to support construction from detached Window settings?",
